Version 1.1.0:
Release Date: 11/11/2026

INFO - Added a sudden-death game mode and GPLv3 licensing.

  - Added Sudden Death mode, where losing one life ends the game immediately.
  - Added the GNU General Public License version 3.
  - Added command-line help, info, game start, game mode, and user-data commands.
  - Added command-line difficulty selection.
  - Randomized the answer order for each question while keeping the correct answer mapping accurate.
  - Fixed a shuffle index bound that could cause an out-of-range crash.
  - Renamed the executable from main to entropy.
  - Added an installer for placing entropy on the system PATH.

Version 1.0.0:
Release Date: 09/11/2026 - 3:41 PM

INFO - Initial release of the application

  - First version with logging functionality implemented.
  - Added highscore, question data and user data saving and loading functionality.
  - Added basic user interface for displaying scores and questions.
  - Implemented basic error handling for file operations.

  - Details of this file:
    - This log file records the version history of the application.
    - Each entry includes the version number, date, and a summary of changes made in that version.
    - The log is intended to help developers and users track the evolution of the application over time.

GENERAL INFORMATION:
  - Game go kaboom! There is no GUI, only a console interface. You don't need to know more!
  - Developed in a MacBook Air M1 running macOS Tahoe 26, not to flex!
  - I may add GUI support later.
  - Version 1.0.0 is the first version of the game.
  - Cross-platform is NOT tested, although it's probably easy to add support.
  - Uses Nim and JSON.
  - Version increments by 0.0.1 for minor changes, 0.1.0 for new features, and 1.0.0 for major releases.